# Post-production ship rule

After every completed production cycle (feature mission, fix mission, or release-ready change set that was committed):

1. **Push to GitHub** for the repo that changed (`git push -u origin HEAD` on the working branch). Do not skip this unless the user explicitly says not to push.
2. **Deploy the live surfaces**:
   - **mybrandOS** → Railway production (project/service already linked; prefer Railway MCP `deploy` or GitHub-triggered deploy). Confirm deployment health.
   - **Public branded delivery** → Netlify on **LIFEOS PORTAL** when Portal config/proxy/edge changed, or when a Netlify rebuild is needed so `*.getlifeos.app` picks up upstream changes. If only mybrandOS backend/app changed and Portal is unchanged, Railway deploy is enough for app runtime; still note Netlify status.
3. Report the **GitHub commit URL / SHA**, **Railway deployment status**, and **Netlify status** (or “unchanged / not required”) in the wrap-up.
4. Never force-push `main`/`master`. Never deploy secrets in commit messages.

This is standing user preference: ship after every production circle, not only when asked mid-cycle.
